Summary:
---------

Context in https://github.com/react-native-community/cli/issues/1348#issue-787562729 and https://github.com/react-native-community/cli/issues/1348#issuecomment-763234781

Note that react-native 0.63 (which uses cli@4.x) already uses the 0.59 versions of various metro packages: https://github.com/facebook/react-native/blob/27651720b40cab564a0cbd41be56a02584e0c73a/package.json#L101-L103


Test Plan:
----------

I initialized a new react-native@0.63 project, cherry-picked #1350 on to this branch to test it together with this, and followed the CONTRIBUTING instructions to run the local version of the CLI in the new project. I was able to successfully use this code in App.js:

```
try {
  require('does-not-exist');
} catch {
  console.log('failed to import');
}
```

<img width="827" alt="Screen Shot 2021-01-20 at 9 19 42 PM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/90494/105283392-37beae80-5b65-11eb-927f-b57b644cbb1d.png">

A little experiment, to test rule naming convention through an ordinary Go test, by parsing the AST and verifying the convention from there.

- Rule ID: [A-Z]{3}[0-9]{3}
- Filename of single rule: ruleID.toLower() + ".go", i.e. [a-z]{3}[0-9]{3}.go
- ValidationFn name: "Validate" + rule name as [A-Z][A-Z]{2}[0-9]{3}
- Bonus: call to NewRule has matching ruleID and ValidationFn name
- README update with corresponding section

This is a followup on https://github.com/liferay-frontend/liferay-portal/pull/639 and https://github.com/liferay-frontend/liferay-portal/pull/713. See details about the renaming in https://github.com/liferay-frontend/liferay-portal/pull/713#issue-558236868

The change in this PR is based on https://github.com/brianchandotcom/liferay-portal/pull/97913#issuecomment-764516581

