This PR adds unit tests for the formatter. Moving the json in the message to the top level feature is not in the formatter yet, but it is tested here. It will be added in a future PR with all the refactoring changes, together with comparison screenshots of the formatting changes. These are the preliminary notes for the test cases:
```
 - { ... , severity: "FATAL" , ... } should now be { ... , severity: "ERROR", ... }
 - "Status 200" messages should be parsed to { status: 200 }
 - "GET http://fsa-rp-test.epimorphics.net/..." messages should be parsed to { method: "GET", path: "http://fsa-rp-test.epimorphics.net/..." }
 - "User-Agent: \"Faraday v1.3.0\"\nAccept: \"application/json\"" messages should be parsed to { user_agent:"Faraday v1.3.0", accept:"application/json" }
 - "2020-12-15T20:15:21 . 495593 " timestamp should now be correctly parsed and formatted as { ..., timestamp: "2020-12-15 20:15:21", ... }
 - all messages are going to be flat json, so this: { severity: "INFO", timestamp: "...", message: { status: 200 } } should turn into this: { severity: "INFO", timestamp: "...", status: 200 } (this should guarantee message can only be a string or missing)
```

